\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces Corrected implementation (v3), internal validation. Single models report the best epoch of the EMA weights or their SWA, without test-time augmentation unless stated. ``Flip'' averages the prediction with that of the horizontally flipped image. The greedy ensemble is a uniform average of three models chosen by forward selection on this validation fold, so it is optimistic; the fixed four-model average has no selection. The two Markov Prior rows average four models (two seeds, original run and rerun) with the patient-history Markov prior of Section~\ref {sec:markov} either supplied or zeroed; ``history withheld'' is the condition of the test set. The rows above them contain no Markov component. The Mixture-of-Experts row is the published value of our challenge submission~\cite  {b12} (Table~\ref {tab1}), measured at 384~px with no seed repeats and not re-evaluated here, so its differences from the other rows include the change of input resolution. The row marked ``official test set'' is the final CXR-LT Task~1 test-set score of the same submission~\cite  {b12} (Table~3 there; mECE not reported); it is on different images from every other row, which are internal validation, and must not be compared with them. -- = not computed or not reported.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab3}{{III}{6}{}{table.3}{}}
