\newlabel{eq:transition}{{8}{7}{}{equation.8}{}}
\newlabel{eq:smoothing}{{9}{7}{}{equation.9}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VI-B}}Route B: Transitions Across a Patient's Studies}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:mk-patient}{{\mbox  {VI-B}}{7}{}{subsection.6.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Route (A): part of the label-to-label Markov chain $P$ of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:transition}, estimated on the training fold (103,305 images; training counts in brackets). Each arrow $i \to j$ is labelled with $P_{ij}$, the share of label $i$'s co-occurrences that involve $j$. For the three tail findings and for Normal, the two largest entries of the row are drawn, and for Support Devices and the catheter the largest one. Orange: tail ($<1\%$ prevalence), blue: medium, violet: head. One random-walk step (Eq.~\eqref  {eq:smoothing}) moves predicted probability along the arrows, from $i$ to $j$, so out of the rare findings and into the common ones. The reverse entries are small, because a common finding's row is spread over many partners: $P$ from pleural effusion to hydropneumothorax is 0.0007, and from Support Devices to pneumothorax 0.0068. $P$ is also asymmetric (Support Devices $\to $ catheter 0.214, catheter $\to $ Support Devices 0.345). The Normal row is built from only the few images where Normal co-occurs with a finding (34 with cardiomegaly), yet must sum to one, so $P$ cannot express that Normal excludes every finding.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cooc}{{5}{7}{}{figure.5}{}}
\newlabel{eq:chain}{{10}{7}{}{equation.10}{}}
\newlabel{eq:emission}{{11}{7}{}{equation.11}{}}
\citation{b14}
\citation{b23}
\newlabel{eq:init}{{12}{8}{}{equation.12}{}}
\newlabel{eq:trans}{{13}{8}{}{equation.13}{}}
\newlabel{eq:fuse}{{14}{8}{}{equation.14}{}}
\newlabel{eq:qw}{{15}{8}{}{equation.15}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The post-prediction patient HMM as a graphical model, with one state per patient and date. Orange circles are the hidden finding states $y_t \in \{0,1\}^{30}$, blue boxes the images and the frozen classifier, white boxes metadata. The transition prior $\pi $ (Eq.~\eqref  {eq:trans}) depends on the previous state, the metadata of the current date and the gap $\Delta _t$; a state without an earlier state uses $\pi ^{0}(m)$ (Eq.~\eqref  {eq:init}). The classifier supplies only the emission (Eq.~\eqref  {eq:emission}), and prior and emission are combined after the network. In the observed mode $y_{t-1}$ is read from the previous report (dashed); in the filtered mode it is inferred from $x_{1:t-1}$ by a forward pass over the patient's earlier images.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hmm}{{6}{8}{}{figure.6}{}}
