\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Association between metadata fields (columns) and the 30 labels (rows, ordered by training prevalence, most frequent at the top) on the training fold. Colour is Cram\'er's $V$ from white (0) to dark blue (0.53); values of 0.15 and above are printed. The study-level fields are acuity, projection, time gap, age, number of earlier studies, sex and year; the remaining columns are acquisition fields (scanner resolution, relative exposure, exposure time, tube current, image rows, manufacturer, modality).}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
